<h3 class="flex whitespace-pre-wrap group font-semibold" id="why-does-my-worker-have-an-unsupported-status" aria-labelledby="_R_2r5deehkd74t9_"><div class="absolute" tabindex="-1"><a href="#why-does-my-worker-have-an-unsupported-status" class="-ml-10 flex items-center opacity-0 border-0 group-hover:opacity-100 focus:opacity-100 focus:outline-0 group/link" aria-label="Navigate to header: Why Does My Worker Have an Unsupported Status?">​<div class="size-6 rounded-md flex items-center justify-center shadow-xs text-gray-400 dark:text-white/50 dark:bg-background-dark dark:brightness-[1.35] dark:ring-1 dark:hover:brightness-150 bg-white ring-1 ring-gray-400/30 dark:ring-gray-700/25 hover:ring-gray-400/60 dark:hover:ring-white/20 group-focus/link:border-2 group-focus/link:border-primary dark:group-focus/link:border-primary-light"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="18" height="18" stroke-width="2" class="size-3 shrink-0"><use href="#mi-mint-1-Link"></use></svg></div></a></div><span id="_R_2r5deehkd74t9_" class="cursor-pointer">Why Does My Worker Have an Unsupported Status?</span></h3>
<span data-as="p">This occurs when your GPU/CPU is not listed among the supported devices on the IO Network. You can check the list of supported devices <a href="/docs/guides/workers/supported-devices" class="link">here</a>.</span>
